# What NOT to upload to Cloud Build.
#
# Without this file the whole directory goes up — including .venv, which is a
# Windows virtualenv roughly a hundred times larger than the application it
# supports. It cannot run on the Linux base image, so it is pure upload cost
# on every deploy, and `COPY . .` would bake it into the shipped layer too.
#
# Note this file is NOT the same as .dockerignore: gcloud reads this one when
# staging the source, Docker reads that one when building. Both exist, and
# both have to list .venv, or whichever is missing lets it back in.

.venv/
.venv-*/
venv/
build/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Local-only state and secrets. .env points at the emulator; shipping it would
# have production quietly try to reach a database on someone's laptop.
.env
.env.*
var/
*.log

# The test suite needs the Firestore emulator, which does not exist in the
# image. Nothing runs it there.
tests/
